---
title: "Reel: the night watch"
note: "A three-clip ref2va reel that keeps a face: the first clip opens on the keeper's face, and SEND makes that frame image 1 for every later clip, so the lamp room and the ship still know him after the stairs end on his back. Generate ×3 plays it (Orrery Continue / Orrery Film, or H3 Motion Context); wire the picks into Orrery Refs and its ref_N into Reference to Video. No input image: image 1 comes from the reel itself."
tags: [h3, reel, ref2va, send, motion_context]
---
@h3 ref2va 16:9 lite
style: live-action, cinematic
context: 22
$storm = {a rising gale|a heavy sea fog|a thunderstorm rolling in from the sea}

MUSIC: a low, sustained cello drone at a slow tempo

CAST
KEEPER (image 1): an old lighthouse keeper, in a yellow oilskin coat and a knitted cap

CHUNK the stairs
SHOT 8s: tracking, slow
KEEPER's weathered face is lit by his lantern as he looks up the iron spiral stairs of the lighthouse; then he turns and climbs them while $storm batters the tower.
SFX: boots ring on iron steps; wind howls against the walls
HANDOFF: KEEPER reaches the small door of the lamp room at the top of the stairs
SEND: frame 0 to image 1

CHUNK the lamp
SHOT 7s: push in, small, slow
KEEPER opens the door and lights the great lamp; the lens begins to turn and throws a sweeping beam out into $storm.
SFX: a match strikes; gears grind as the lens starts to turn
HANDOFF: the sweeping beam passes over the dark sea

CHUNK the ship
SHOT 8s: pull out, slow
Far below, the beam finds a small fishing boat fighting the waves, and the boat turns toward the light.
SFX: waves crash against the rocks; a distant ship's horn answers
